 copies would compute different policies. Under the shared prior before observation, which instance is \"me\" is uncertain, so cooperating on both comes out best.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a prisoner's dilemma between two copies that see different inputs, so under P-FDT I should pick a single policy mapping each input to an action. The policy space pairs an action for Rowan's observation with one for Sasha's, and since neither copy knows which it is, the prior is symmetric. Checking the candidate where both stay quiet, each copy's expected outcome comes to two years.\n\nI'm checking the case where each copy evaluates from its own position: if Rowan evaluates as Rowan, defecting on its own input and cooperating on the other looks best, but Sasha would reason the same way, so the copies would compute different policies. Under the shared prior before observation, which instance is \"me\" is uncertain, so cooperating on both comes out best.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9630,"completion_tokens":824,"total_tokens":10454,"cost":0.055,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.055,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03852,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01648},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":492,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}